                    "A PARTICIPLE turns a verb into an",
                    "adjective. Its vowel tells the time,",
                    "as in -as, -is, -os:",
                    "A = now, I = before, O = later.",
                    "",
                    "THE ONE DOING IT (legi = read):       Press 1",
                    "-anta = doing now     leganta = reading",
                    "-inta = having done   leginta = having read",
                    "-onta = about to do   legonta = about to read",
                    "",
                    "THE THING IT IS DONE TO:              Press 2",
                    "-ata  = being done    legata  = being read",
                    "-ita  = done          legita  = read",
                    "-ota  = to be done    legota  = to be read"
